## Impact

The identified vulnerabilities can result in:

* Unauthorized access to other users' data
* Authentication bypass
* Account compromise
* Unauthorized user deletion
* Manipulation of protected application data
* Internal network access through SSRF
* Resource exhaustion through oversized uploads
* Brute-force account compromise
* Exposure of internal application information
* Extended validity of compromised authentication tokens

## Remediation

* Implement server-side object-level and function-level authorization
* Validate and sanitize all user-controlled input
* Prevent NoSQL operator injection using strict schema validation
* Enforce a single, explicitly configured JWT signing algorithm
* Never expose stack traces or internal errors to clients
* Apply strict allowlists for object properties
* Validate and restrict server-side URL requests
* Enforce server-side file size and upload restrictions
* Maintain an accurate API inventory and remove unused endpoints
* Implement rate limiting and account lockout controls
* Use short-lived access tokens with appropriate token rotation and revocation

